solutions.latex:
Shape:

Beth's scores are positively skewed; Amy's scores are symmetrical.

Summary statistics (any one of):

the median score for Amy is $40$, whereas Beth's median is $30$;

$75\%$ of Amy's scores are higher than $30$ but only $50\%$ of Beth's scores are higher than $30$;

$25\%$ of both Amy's and Beth's scores are higher than $50$.

Spread (any one or all of):

Beth has a larger range than Amy;

Beth has a larger IQR than Amy;

so Amy is more consistent than Beth.

